{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridgeEquation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridgeEquation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Derivation.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.AlienBridgeEquation"],"declarations":52,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.monomial_eigenvalue_mem_zpowers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.monomial_eigenvalue_mem_zpowers","kind":"theorem","line":599,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L599-L615","doc":"**A prune: the monomial grading carries no q-bridge weight.**\n\nThe dilation acts on the monomial `x^{n}` with eigenvalue `qⁿ`, and every\n`qⁿ` lies in `q^ℤ` — the *identity* class of `E_q = ℂ*/q^ℤ`.  So on the index\nset of monomial `σ`-eigenvalue **classes** there is only one class: the shift\nis trivially the identity, `untwist` applies for an empty reason, and no\nweight distinguishes anything.\n\n**Reading — scope-(a), a where-not-to-look result, not a computation.**\nWhatever q-bridge weight a q-difference module carries, it is not visible in\nthe monomial grading of its formal solution.  For C1's `∞` side the weight\nwould have to come from the *quadratic* factor certified by\n`deg_q(cₙ) = n²` (`QOU.QBeta.cCoeff_natDegree`), not from the powers of `x`.\nNothing here says the weight is trivial, or that C1 has no weight; it says\nthis particular grading cannot exhibit one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.shift_mul_eq_id_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.shift_mul_eq_id_iff","kind":"theorem","line":585,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L585-L597","doc":"**On `ℂ*` the twist is unavoidable.**  For singularity locations forming a\ngroup and `shift ω = q·ω`, the shift is the identity **iff `q = 1`**.  So for a\ngenuine dilation (`q ≠ 1`) no untwisted `QBridgeSystem` on that index set\nexists, and one must pass to the spiral quotient.  This is the precise sense\nin which `E_q` is forced rather than chosen. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.toTwisted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.toTwisted","kind":"def","line":574,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L574-L583","doc":"Every untwisted system is a twisted one with `shift = id`, so nothing proved\nabout `QBridgeSystem` is lost. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem.untwist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem.untwist","kind":"def","line":558,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L558-L570","doc":"**The twist vanishes exactly when the alien family is shift-invariant.**\n\n`hinv` says the family is constant along the orbit of `shift` — for the\ndilation, constant along q-spirals, i.e. factoring through `E_q = ℂ*/q^ℤ`.\nUnder it the twisted system *is* an untwisted `QBridgeSystem`, with the same\ndata. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem.conjDeriv_iterate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem.conjDeriv_iterate","kind":"theorem","line":536,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L536-L556","doc":"**Weights accumulate along the orbit.**  Conjugating `n` times walks the index\nalong `shift` and multiplies the weights encountered on the way:\n\n`σⁿ ∘ Δ_ω ∘ σ⁻ⁿ = (∏_{k<n} c_{shiftᵏ ω}) · Δ_{shiftⁿ ω}`.\n\nThis is the content of the twist.  When `shift = id` it collapses to\n`c_ω ⁿ · Δ_ω`, recovering the untwisted picture; when `shift` is a genuine\ndilation of the Borel plane the index genuinely moves, and the product is over\na whole q-spiral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem.bridge_deriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem.bridge_deriv","kind":"theorem","line":527,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L527-L534","doc":"The bridge at the level of derivations, in the semisimple case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem.IsSemisimple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem.IsSemisimple","kind":"def","line":524,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L524-L525","doc":"No unipotent part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem.bridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem.bridge","kind":"theorem","line":518,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L518-L518","doc":"The twisted q-bridge equation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem.unipotent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem.unipotent","kind":"def","line":516,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L516-L516","doc":"The nilpotent part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem.shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem.shift","kind":"def","line":514,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L514-L514","doc":"The induced motion of the singularity index (`ω ↦ qω` for a dilation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem.weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem.weight","kind":"def","line":512,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L512-L512","doc":"The multiplicative weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem.alien","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem.alien","kind":"def","line":510,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L510-L510","doc":"The alien derivation at `ω`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem.dil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem.dil","kind":"def","line":508,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L508-L508","doc":"The dilation automorphism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem.mk","kind":"ctor","line":505,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L505-L505","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.TwistedQBridgeSystem","kind":"structure","line":503,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L503-L520","doc":"A **twisted** q-bridge system: like `QBridgeSystem`, but the conjugation may\nmove the singularity index by `shift`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.polyUnipotentSystem_not_isSemisimple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.polyUnipotentSystem_not_isSemisimple","kind":"theorem","line":464,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L464-L470","doc":"**The `unipotent` field is not decorative.**  A concrete system whose adjoint\naction is a genuine Jordan block: the semisimple weight is `1`, so\n`qweight_shift_of_semisimple` does not apply, and the correction term in\n`qweight_shift` is `d/dX ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.polyUnipotentSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.polyUnipotentSystem","kind":"def","line":456,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L456-L462","doc":"**The concrete mixed system.**  `R[X]`, the shift `X ↦ X + 1`, `Δ := X·d/dX`.\nIts adjoint action under the shift is `Δ ↦ Δ + d/dX`: weight `1`, unipotent\npart `d/dX`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.polyDerivation_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.polyDerivation_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":448,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L448-L454","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.shift_conj_derivative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.shift_conj_derivative","kind":"theorem","line":435,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L435-L446","doc":"`d/dX` is invariant under the shift — the concrete form of `hcomm`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.shiftAlgEquiv_X","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.shiftAlgEquiv_X","kind":"theorem","line":430,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L430-L433","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.shiftAlgEquiv_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.shiftAlgEquiv_apply","kind":"theorem","line":427,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L427-L428","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.shiftAlgEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.shiftAlgEquiv","kind":"def","line":418,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L418-L425","doc":"The shift automorphism `X ↦ X + 1` of `R[X]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.unipotentSystem_not_isSemisimple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.unipotentSystem_not_isSemisimple","kind":"theorem","line":404,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L404-L410","doc":"**The mixed model really is mixed.**  Whenever `D ≠ 0` the system is not\nsemisimple, so `QBridgeSystem`'s `unipotent` field is not decorative and\n`qweight_shift`'s correction term is not always zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.unipotentSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.unipotentSystem","kind":"def","line":383,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L383-L402","doc":"**A mixed (non-semisimple) q-bridge system.**  With `σ t = t + 1` — the\nq-logarithm relation — and `σ ∘ D ∘ σ⁻¹ = D`, the single alien derivation\n`Δ := t·D` satisfies\n\n`σ ∘ Δ ∘ σ⁻¹ = 1 · Δ + D`,\n\ni.e. multiplicative weight `1` and unipotent part `D`.  The adjoint action is\na Jordan block: it fixes the eigenvalue and adds a nilpotent shift. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.polyQEuler_weights","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.polyQEuler_weights","kind":"theorem","line":356,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L356-L368","doc":"**The additive-vs-multiplicative theorem, concretely witnessed.**  On `R[X]`\nthe same family `Δ_n = Xⁿ·(X·d/dX)`, on the same index `n`, has classical\nweight `n` against the Euler *derivation* and q-weight `cⁿ` against the\n*dilation*.  Both hypotheses of\n`euler_weight_additive_qweight_multiplicative` hold here simultaneously, so\nthat theorem is not vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.polyQEulerSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.polyQEulerSystem","kind":"def","line":349,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L349-L354","doc":"**The concrete q-difference bridge system**: `R[X]`, dilation `X ↦ c·X`,\n`Δ_n := Xⁿ·(X·d/dX)`, multiplicative weight `cⁿ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.dilate_comm_polyEuler","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.dilate_comm_polyEuler","kind":"theorem","line":340,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L340-L347","doc":"The dilation commutes with the Euler operator — both are degree operators.\nSupplies `qEulerSystem`'s second hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.dilateAlgEquiv_X","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.dilateAlgEquiv_X","kind":"theorem","line":335,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L335-L338","doc":"The dilation scales `X` by `c`.  Supplies `qEulerSystem`'s first hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.polyEuler_X","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.polyEuler_X","kind":"theorem","line":329,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L329-L333","doc":"`X` is an Euler coordinate: `E X = X`.  Supplies `AlienBridge.eulerSystem`'s\nhypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.polyEuler_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.polyEuler_apply","kind":"theorem","line":326,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L326-L327","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.polyEuler","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.polyEuler","kind":"def","line":321,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L321-L324","doc":"The **Euler operator** `X·d/dX` on `R[X]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.dilateAlgEquiv_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.dilateAlgEquiv_apply","kind":"theorem","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L318-L319","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.dilateAlgEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.dilateAlgEquiv","kind":"def","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L298-L316","doc":"The dilation automorphism `X ↦ c·X` of `R[X]`, for a unit `c`.  This is the\nalgebraic q-dilation `σ_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.euler_weight_additive_qweight_multiplicative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.euler_weight_additive_qweight_multiplicative","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L259-L288","doc":"**The answer, stated as one theorem.**  Suppose the *same* `(A, E, t)` carries\nboth structures — `E t = t` (so `AlienBridge.eulerSystem` applies) and\n`σ t = c·t` with `σ` commuting with `E` (so `qEulerSystem` applies).  Then:\n\n* the two systems have the **same alien family** `Δ_n = tⁿ·E`, indexed by the\n  same `n`;\n* the classical weight is **`n`** — additive;\n* the q-weight is **`cⁿ`** — multiplicative.\n\nSo additive and multiplicative are not rival conventions and not a modelling\nchoice.  There is one grading, indexed by `n`; the classical weight *is* that\nindex, and the q-weight is the multiplicative character `c^{(−)}` evaluated on\nit.  Which one you see is determined by whether the operator you conjugate by\nis a derivation (differentiates the product ⇒ `n` appears additively) or an\nautomorphism (passes through the product ⇒ `cⁿ` appears multiplicatively).\n\nThe general case is neither: `QBridgeSystem` carries a `unipotent` field, and\n`qweight_shift` shows the eigenvalue is then multiplied by the semisimple part\n*and* shifted by the nilpotent one — a Jordan block, the matrix-representation\nform.  Both models here are semisimple; a mixed example needs the q-logarithm,\nwhich is not built. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.qEulerSystem_isSemisimple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.qEulerSystem_isSemisimple","kind":"theorem","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L255-L257","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.qEulerSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.qEulerSystem","kind":"def","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L232-L253","doc":"**The q-Euler bridge system.**  Given a dilation `σ` with `σ t = c · t` and a\nderivation `E` commuting with `σ` (the Euler / degree operator), the family\n`Δ_n := tⁿ·E` satisfies the q-bridge with **multiplicative** weight `cⁿ` and\nno unipotent part.\n\nThe weight comes out multiplicative for a completely explicit reason: `σ` is\nan algebra map, so it passes through the product `tⁿ · E(−)` and multiplies\nby `σ(t)ⁿ = cⁿ`.  A derivation would instead have *differentiated* the\nproduct and produced `n` additively. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.alien_eq_zero_of_dil_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.alien_eq_zero_of_dil_comm","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L207-L226","doc":"**The hypothesis has teeth.**  If `σ` commutes with `Δ_ω` (the conjugation is\ntrivial) and the system is semisimple, then every value of `Δ_ω` is fixed by\nscaling by `c_ω`.  So whenever `c_ω` fixes nothing but `0`, commutation forces\n`Δ_ω = 0`.\n\nNote the degenerate value is `c_ω = 1`, not `c_ω = 0` — the multiplicative\ncounterpart of the classical `ω = 0` (`AlienBridge.ord_comm_of_weight_zero`),\nand a check that the weight really does sit in the relation multiplicatively.\nThe hypothesis is phrased as \"scaling by `c_ω` fixes only `0`\" rather than\n\"`c_ω − 1` acts injectively\" so that it stays over a `CommSemiring`, where\nthere is no subtraction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.qweight_mul_of_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.qweight_mul_of_comp","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L187-L205","doc":"**Weights MULTIPLY under composition** (diagonal case) — the q-analogue of\n`AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.weight_add_of_comp`, where they add.  So the `Δ_ω`\ngenerate an algebra graded by a *multiplicative* character group rather than\nby an additive one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.qweight_shift_of_semisimple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.qweight_shift_of_semisimple","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L178-L185","doc":"**The diagonal case: purely multiplicative.**  With no unipotent part the\n`σ`-eigenvalue is simply scaled by the weight: `λ ↦ c_ω · λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.qweight_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.qweight_shift","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L153-L176","doc":"**The weight shift is MULTIPLICATIVE, with a unipotent correction.**\n\nIf `f` is a `σ`-eigenvector of eigenvalue `λ` (a unit), then\n\n`σ(Δ_ω f) = (c_ω · λ) · Δ_ω f  +  λ · N_ω f`.\n\nThis is the combined / matrix-representation form: the semisimple part\n**multiplies** the eigenvalue by `c_ω`, and the unipotent part contributes an\nadditive correction — a Jordan block rather than a diagonal entry.  Contrast\n`AlienBridge.BridgeSystem.weight_shift`, where conjugating by a *derivation*\ngives `λ ↦ λ + ω`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.dil_alien_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.dil_alien_symm","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L148-L151","doc":"Solved form: `σ(Δ_ω(σ⁻¹ f)) = c_ω · Δ_ω f + N_ω f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.IsSemisimple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.IsSemisimple","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L145-L146","doc":"The adjoint action is diagonalisable — no unipotent part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.bridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.bridge","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L140-L140","doc":"The q-bridge equation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.unipotent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.unipotent","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L138-L138","doc":"The nilpotent part of the adjoint action (zero in the diagonalisable case). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.weight","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L136-L136","doc":"The **multiplicative** weight — the semisimple part of the adjoint action. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.alien","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.alien","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L134-L134","doc":"The alien derivation at the singularity `ω`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.dil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.dil","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L132-L132","doc":"The dilation automorphism `σ` (classically `x ↦ qx`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem.mk","kind":"ctor","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L129-L129","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.QBridgeSystem","kind":"structure","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L113-L141","doc":"A **q-native bridge system**: a dilation automorphism `σ`, a family of alien\nderivations `Δ_ω`, a **multiplicative** weight `c_ω`, a unipotent correction,\nand the relation\n\n`σ ∘ Δ_ω ∘ σ⁻¹ = c_ω · Δ_ω + N_ω`.\n\nThe relation is a **field**, i.e. a hypothesis — nothing in the data\ndetermines it, and axiomatising it would not establish it (AGENTS.md\n§\"Axiomatization is NOT a Proof\").\n\nThe `unipotent` field is what makes this the general \"combined\" form: the\nadjoint action of `σ` on the `Δ_ω` need not be diagonalisable, and the Levi\ndecomposition of a local q-difference Galois group is precisely a torus of\nmultiplicative characters extended by a unipotent part ([vanderput2006]\n§5 (1), (5); the `Δ_ω` themselves are [ramis-sauloy2006] Thm 3.5).  Setting\n`unipotent = 0` (`IsSemisimple`) recovers the pure multiplicative case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.conjDeriv_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.conjDeriv_smul","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L105-L109","doc":"Conjugation is `R`-linear in the derivation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.conjDeriv_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.conjDeriv_apply","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L101-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.conjDeriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QAlienBridge.conjDeriv","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QAlienBridgeEquation.lean#L88-L99","doc":"`σ ∘ D ∘ σ⁻¹` is again a derivation.  Mathlib has `Derivation` and\n`AlgEquiv` but does not provide this conjugation, which is the whole content\nof the q-side bridge relation: in the q-setting the \"ordinary operator\" is an\nautomorphism, so the relation is a conjugation rather than a commutator. ","signatureChunk":0}]}